HA funding opportunities\nScope of our grants\nPrecision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\nTuesday, May 6, 2025\nEHA Mentorship Program\nMenu\nClose\nConnect & Network\nEHA2027 Congress\nEHA2027 registration\nEHA2027 program\nEHA2027 abstract submission\nEHA2027 travel grants & abstract awards\nEHA2027 sponsorship opportunities\nEHA2027 details and deadlines\nEHA2027 sustainability\nEHA2026 Congress\nEHA2026 Congress platform\nEHA2026 sustainability\nCongress archive\nEHA2026 Perspectives Congress Report\nEHA2026 gallery\nEHA2025 Perspectives Congress Reports\nEHA2025 gallery\nEHA2024 Chair's wrap-up\nEHA2024 report\nEHA2024 gallery\nEHA2023 report\nEHA2023 gallery\nScientific meetings\nMembership\nFull membership\nJunior membership\nTrial membership\nHealthcare-affiliated professional membership\nEmeritus membership\nJoint EHA and national society membership\nUsing MyEHA\nClinical practice\nOur guidelines initiative\nGuidelines by areas of disease\nEHA Guidelines app\nEHA Clinical Guidelines Webinar Series\nBedside Hematology – Rapid Reference\nEducation & Training\nEHA Campus\nLearning paths\nEuropean Hematology Curriculum\nEntrustable Professional Activities\nLighting the Flame Program\nTests and tools\nEHA Diagnosis\nEHA Exam\nProgress Test\nMentoring and career development\nCareer comparison tool\nEHA Mentorship Program\nMaster Class\nResearch training programs\nEHA-EMBO Lab Leadership Course\nResearch & Innovation\nHemaSphere\nSpecialized Working Groups\nSupport for SWG scientific meetings\nSWG Grants\nHow to apply to join an SWG\nWebinars and online groups\nSWG Preceptorship Program\nGrants\nEHA Research Grants\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\nEHA Innovation Grant\nEHA Kick-off Grant\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\nEHA Travel Grants\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\nScope of our grants\nTopics-in-Focus program\nPrecision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\nCongress\nHemaSphere\nAbout EHA\nSearch\nJoin EHA\nLogin\nHome\nAbout EHA\nWork at EHA\nJobs that match your ambition\nEHA is a not-for-profit organization that’s on a mission to transform hematology by mobilizing the community, sharing knowledge, and connecting interests. We advocate for hematology in Europe—and beyond. We seek team members, based in the Netherlands, who are creative, driven to achieve excellence, and inspired by our vision of achieving Borderless Hematology.\nHead of Education\nOctober 30, 2026\nHybrid\nAre you experienced in CME development and up-to-date with educational programs, and ready to join a vibrant association serving 12.000 members? Join EHA as Head of Education.\nSee vacancy\nTemp. Membership Engagement Manager\nOctober 23, 2026\nHybrid\nWorking at the heart of membership engagement? Apply and join EHA as Membership Engagement Manager.\nSee vacancy\nEHA Intern – Program Management\nOctober 21, 2026\nHybrid\nAn international internship opportunity where you will support the Senior Program Manager in charge of Congress and Scientific Meetings.\nSee vacancy\nEHA Internship – Open Application\nJuly 12, 2026\nHybrid\nAre you looking for an internship opportunity where you make a positive impact to the international Hematology landscape?\nSee vacancy\n“At EHA, each voice matters, each idea is valued, and together we strive to transform the landscape of hematology—empowering progress, advancing discovery, and building a future where care knows no borders.”\nRob\nHead of Operations\n“After losing my dad to leukemia in 2024, I felt eager to use my skills and experience to make a meaningful impact for patients, caregivers, and doctors in the field of hematology. I am incredibly grateful for the opportunity to work at EHA, and I am passionate about the positive impact we create with our work.”\nLaura\nProject Manager, Education\nJoin EHA\nFull membership\nJunior membership\n60-day trial\nGet involved\nCareer development\nScientific meetings\nAbout us\nMission and vision\nJobs\nSponsor EHA\nContact us\nFollow us\nPrivacy statement\nTerms and conditions\nSubscribe\nCopyright © 2026\nBecome an EHA Mentor\nEHA Mentorship Program\nDiscover the rewards of mentoring\nApply by October 29\nApply today",
